# Force LF line endings for all text files on checkout, regardless of a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting - a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite committed LF to CRLF, which
# breaks any test that reads a checked-in text fixture (e.g. a golden JSON
# snapshot) and compares it byte-for-byte against in-memory-generated
# content (which always uses LF, e.g. Jackson's pretty printer). See
# McpContractSnapshotTest / McpOutputContractSnapshotTest and issue #15.
* text=auto eol=lf

# mvnw.cmd is a genuine Windows batch script (committed with CRLF, matching
# the upstream Maven Wrapper distribution) - fully excluded from the
# blanket LF rule above (not just re-pointed at eol=crlf, which still
# round-trips the file through LF normalization first) so git leaves its
# checked-in bytes untouched.
mvnw.cmd -text
